IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited -- Hospital Income Policy`

-- Rules only. No claim data is defined in this file -- see apply.l4 for the
-- nine benchmark claims that get run against these rules.
--
-- Two simplifications, both required by the task brief:
--   * Section 1.1's conditions 1 (agreement signed) and 2 (premium paid) are
--     assumed always satisfied, so no fields or rules encode them.
--   * Every date/time fact in a claim, other than the claimant's age, is
--     expressed as a NUMBER OF MONTHS AFTER THE POLICY'S EFFECTIVE DATE, so
--     no DATE type or date arithmetic is needed anywhere in this file.

§§ `The shape of a claim`

DECLARE Claim HAS
    `age at hospitalization`                                                      IS A NUMBER
    -- how long after the effective date the hospitalization happened; used both
    -- for the Section 1.3 "still pending" test and the Section 4.6 term test.
    `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred`                IS A NUMBER
    `due to sickness`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `due to accidental injury`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Section 2.2: the daily benefit is only payable for confinement in a
    -- hospital in the United States. This is narrower than Section 4.1.1's
    -- worldwide insuring scope -- see the note at `confined in hospital as a
    -- result of sickness or accidental injury` below.
    `hospital located in the United States`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- Section 3.1(1)-(4): each flag means the sickness/injury arose directly or
    -- indirectly out of that activity -- not merely that the claimant held that
    -- occupation or status at the time. Being a firefighter, soldier, or police
    -- officer WHEN hospitalized, for an unrelated cause, does not set the
    -- matching flag; see apply.l4's q9 for a worked example of the distinction.
    `caused by skydiving`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by service in the military`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by service as a fire fighter`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused by service in the police`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- NOTHING means no confirmation has been supplied (yet). JUST n means
    -- confirmation was supplied n months after the effective date.
    `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`               IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `1. Policy in effect and conditions`

-- Section 1.3, first disjunct of 1.1(3): written confirmation of the wellness
-- visit was supplied no later than the 7th month anniversary of the effective
-- date. (This encoding tests only the confirmation's own submission date
-- against the 7-month deadline; see NOTES.md for why the separate 6-month
-- "visit itself" deadline is not modelled as an independent fact.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wellness visit confirmation supplied in a timely fashion` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN n AT MOST 7

-- Section 1.3, second disjunct of 1.1(3): no confirmation has been supplied
-- yet, but the 7-month deadline (measured as of the hospitalization) has not
-- passed either, so the condition is still open rather than failed.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1.3 condition still pending` IF
    CONSIDER claim's `months after the effective date the wellness visit confirmation was supplied`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred` AT MOST 7
    WHEN JUST n  THEN FALSE

-- Section 1.1(3): "is still pending or has been satisfied in a timely fashion".
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1.3 condition satisfied` IF
        `wellness visit confirmation supplied in a timely fashion` claim
    OR  `section 1.3 condition still pending` claim

-- Section 4.6: the policy term is one year from the effective date. (Section
-- 1.2 cross-references "Section 5" for the term, but Section 5 is the benefit
-- and premium amounts, not the term -- Section 4.6 is where the term is
-- actually defined, so that is what this rule uses.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy term has expired` IF
    claim's `months after the effective date the hospitalization occurred` GREATER THAN 12

-- Section 1.2: cancelation is deemed to have occurred on any of these grounds.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy has been canceled` IF
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding`
    OR  NOT `section 1.3 condition satisfied` claim
    OR  `policy term has expired` claim

-- Section 1.1: the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization.
-- (Conditions 1 and 2 are assumed satisfied; see the file header.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy in effect at the time of the hospitalization` IF
        `section 1.3 condition satisfied` claim
    AND NOT `policy has been canceled` claim

§§ `2. Benefits`

-- Section 2.1 (the triggering event) combined with Section 2.2's express
-- payability condition (confinement in a hospital in the United States).
-- Section 4.1.1 ("insures You ... anywhere in the world") is reflected
-- elsewhere by the ABSENCE of any territorial exclusion on the underlying
-- risk -- it does not override Section 2.2's narrower condition on when the
-- daily benefit is actually payable. The Section 2.2 365-day cap on the
-- number of payable days is a limit on how much is paid, not on whether the
-- policy applies at all, and no benchmark question turns on confinement
-- length, so it is not modelled as a gate here.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `confined in hospital as a result of sickness or accidental injury` IF
        claim's `hospital located in the United States`
    AND (claim's `due to sickness` OR claim's `due to accidental injury`)

-- Section 2.3: a claim must be made to the Company, setting out the basis for
-- the claim (and for there being no exclusion or cancellation).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `claim properly made to the company` IF
    claim's `claim made to the company with the basis for the claim stated`

§§ `3. General exclusions`

-- Section 3.1(1)-(4): the sickness or accidental injury arises directly or
-- indirectly out of one of these four activities.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an excluded activity caused the hospitalization` IF
        claim's `caused by skydiving`
    OR  claim's `caused by service in the military`
    OR  claim's `caused by service as a fire fighter`
    OR  claim's `caused by service in the police`

-- Section 3.1(5): age at the time of the hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded because of age at hospitalization` IF
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

-- Section 3.1 overall: either kind of exclusion bars the claim.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a general exclusion applies` IF
        `an excluded activity caused the hospitalization` claim
    OR  `excluded because of age at hospitalization` claim

§§ `Top-level coverage decision`

@export Determine whether the Codex Insurance hospital income policy covers a given hospitalization claim
GIVEN claim IS A Claim @desc The hospitalization claim being assessed for coverage under this policy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` IF
        `policy in effect at the time of the hospitalization` claim
    AND `confined in hospital as a result of sickness or accidental injury` claim
    AND `claim properly made to the company` claim
    AND NOT `a general exclusion applies` claim
